# EAS Build (for the e-shop-mobile app) uploads this whole repository.
# Only the mobile app is needed, so everything else is left out. This also avoids
# Laravel's public/storage link, which EAS cannot copy on Windows.
# When this file exists, EAS ignores all .gitignore files, so the mobile app's
# own .gitignore rules are repeated below. Folder rules have no trailing "/" because
# EAS checks paths without one.

/*
!/e-shop-mobile

e-shop-mobile/node_modules
e-shop-mobile/.expo
e-shop-mobile/dist
e-shop-mobile/web-build
e-shop-mobile/expo-env.d.ts
e-shop-mobile/.kotlin
e-shop-mobile/ios
e-shop-mobile/android
*.orig.*
*.jks
*.p8
*.p12
*.key
*.mobileprovision
.metro-health-check*
npm-debug.*
yarn-debug.*
yarn-error.*
.DS_Store
*.pem
.env*.local
*.tsbuildinfo
